<subpara id="RM0000026ZR004X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000DCO00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>A three-way catalytic converter is used to efficiently purify the CO, HC and NOx in the exhaust gas. This three-way catalytic converter functions most efficiently near the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio. For this reason, CO, HC and NOx cannot be efficiently purified unless the engine is accurately controlled near the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio. The air fuel ratio sensor (A/F sensor) is installed for the purpose of this control. The air fuel ratio sensor (A/F sensor) outputs a voltage proportional to the air-fuel ratio, and the engine control computer controls the air-fuel ratio based on that voltage.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A182328J03" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
